FIMPACT — ten-year placebo-surgery comparison (@med-source-fimpact: 0, is #reference, #part-of @medicine-sources) { r_467SRCDKYQD418N93SZG3635D8
Kari Kanto and colleagues, on behalf of the FIMPACT investigators. Arthroscopic subacromial decompression versus placebo surgery for subacromial pain syndrome: 10 year follow-up of the FIMPACT randomised, placebo surgery controlled trial. BMJ 2025;391:e086201. DOI: 10.1136/bmj-2025-086201. English.

[Authorized source](https://www.bmj.com/content/391/bmj-2025-086201).

A primary trial report for the advanced evidence reading. Read the population, allocation, comparison treatments, outcomes, follow-up, uncertainty, and limitations. Its conclusion about decompression in the trial population must not be generalized to every shoulder procedure. [Publisher PDF](https://www.bmj.com/content/391/bmj-2025-086201.full.pdf).

**Access and reuse:** Publisher-hosted free full-text article; no local copy is supplied. Check the article's own licence before redistributing or adapting it. Automated retrieval was blocked during assembly; the official indexed abstract and bibliographic record were available.

